# What's new in Android

## Jetpack Compose
* Autofill: Allows users to automatically fill out form fields with personal information that they have fill out sometime before


* Autosize text: adapts the text to the size of its container, is a parameter in a text composable


* Animate Bounds: Is a modifier that lets you animate the position and the size of a composable in its container and is similar to `animatedContentSize`, but this one animates both size and position at same time


* Visibility tracking: the new modifier called `onLayoutRectChanged` allows you to track a composable's position within either its root, the window, or the screen, is a low level API, useful in use cases related to visibility tracking and position tracking, it is similar to `onGloballyPositioned` but this is more performant out of the box and lets you add throttle or bebouncing which makes it useful for use cases like tracking the location of an item while you're scrolling a lazy list and in the alpha versions of compose some high-level APIs have been added on top of this low level API that are very specific for some use cases. they are the following three items
	* onVisibilityChanged: Is a modifier, gives a callback any time the visibility of a composable changes, useful for stopping or playing a video when it comes into view
	* onFirstVisible: is a modifier, is great for use cases like impression tracking, it gives a callback anytime a composable has been in view for a certain amount of time


* Performance: Latest version of compose hardly has Janks, is a lot more performant and it offers the possibility to make the following optimizations as well:

	* Pausable Composition: Allows to split the composition over several frames
	* Background text Measurement: offloads some of the hard work from the main thread
	* Prefetch customization: Lets you control the prefetching strategy for items in a lazy list


	Because all of these you should know it is important to upgrade to latest version of compose, Google apps like maps are using compose and any changes in compose even for alpha, beta, release candidates are applied to these Google apps within a few days, they are using feature flags to test the changes this means you could also be using features in alpha, beta, etc

