# Unlock user productivity with desktop windowing and stylus support
## Deskot Windowing
This enable on compatible devices when connected to an external display, when a phone is connected to an external display the phone state remains the same and a new desktop session starts on the external display. The phone and the external display operate independently and apps are specific to the display on which they are running, Desktop windowing-enabled devices like tablets will share the same desktop session on both devices, the tablet and the external display, this means you can drag apps from one screen to the other

## Multiple Instances
In Android desktop you can enable multiple instances of your app, you would have to declare it in the manifest like

```
<activity
    android:name=".MainActivity"
    android:exported="true"
    android:label="@string/app_name"
    android:launchMode="singleInstancePerTask"
    android:resizeableActivity="true">

    <!--- This will show a systemUI option to launch a new window --->
    <property
        android:name="android.window.PROERTY_SUPPORTS_MULTI_INSTANCE_SYSTEM_UI"
    android:value="true"/>
</activity>
```

This intent will launch a new instance instead of looking for an existing instance of the app
```
fun startActivityInNewInstance(activity: Activity) {
    val intent = Intent.makeMainActivity(activity.componentName)
    intent.addFlags(Intent.FLAG_ACIVITY_NEW_TASK)
    intent.addFlags(Intent.FLAG_ACIVITY_MULTIPLE_TASK)
    activity.startActivity(intent)
}
```

You can also use drag and drop API form the Compose Foundation library, like when you drag a tab outside from chrome, this creates a new Window

```
modifier = Modifier
    .dragAndDropSource { _ ->
        DragAndDropTransferData(
            clipData = multiInstanceClipData(activity),
            flags = View.DRAG_FLAG_GLOBAL_SAME_APPLICATION or
                    View.DRAG_FLAG_START_INTENT_SENDER_ON_UNHANDLE_DRAG
        )
    }
```

The clipdata is created with the following function

```
fun multiInstanceClipData(activity: Activity): ClipData {
    val intent = Intent.makeMainActivity(activity.componentName)
    val pendingIntent = PendingIntent.getActivity(
            activity, 0, intent, PendingIntent.FLAG_IMMUTABLE
        )
    return ClipData(
        "NewInstance",
        arrayOf(ClipDescription.MIMETYPE_TEX_INTENT),
        ClipData.Item.Builder().setIntentSender(pendingIntent.intentSender).build()
    )
}
```

